From ea83e877dd28425a3fbbbba0e135a7409b3edb3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:44:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVDInputStreamBluray: the second view by its sub-path and the
 angle that plays, under a lock

GetStereoscopicClip() answered with the first clip of any sub play item of the extension
data. Now:

- Only the sub play items of the sub-path of the stereoscopic video count, for the sync id
  and for the position that it falls back to.
- Of a sub play item with a clip for each angle, the clip of the angle that plays is the
  second view (bd_get_current_angle(), taken when the disc reports an angle, a playlist or a
  play item). A play item without that angle shows its first one, as libbluray does; a sub
  play item without a clip for the angle that is shown has no second view.
- It also says which play item it answered for, why there is no second view where there is
  none, and which eye the base view is by the same playlist (Kodi's parser reads the flag
  from the byte that libbluray reads it from; the log has both).

What is known of the playlist is asked for by the thread that demuxes, for every picture,
while the events of the disc are processed by that thread or, for what the user does in a
menu, by the thread of the application. The playlist is now read into a local and exchanged
under a lock that the askers take; the play item and the angle are atomic.

In UpdatePlaylistInformation() the test for "a disc whose second view is read" comes before
everything else: any other disc takes no lock and writes nothing there. A playlist that
cannot be read because there is no path for Kodi's parser is said in the log.

The demuxer passes the new parameters; what it does with them comes next.
---
 .../DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxBluray3D.cpp          |  10 +-
 .../DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.cpp  | 131 ++++++++++++++----
 .../DVDInputStreams/DVDInputStreamBluray.h    |  25 +++-
 3 files changed, 134 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

